  "prediction": "The report discusses the Selected Reserve, a group of over 811,000 part-time military personnel who can be called up for active duty in times of war or national emergency. About 91% of these reservists are part-time, and they train for about 1 weekend a month and 2 weeks a year. The report outlines the different types of training and duties required of reservists, including annual training, monthly drills, and active duty tours. Travel costs for reservists totaled over $925 million in fiscal year 2015, with an average cost of $1,246 per reservist. The report notes that some travel expenses are not reimbursed by the Department of Defense, and officials are considering changes to travel policy to address this issue. The report recommends that the Under Secretary of Defense for Personnel and Readiness collect more data and conduct an analysis of the impact of unreimbursed travel expenses on DOD's budget and readiness.",
  "scored_prediction": "The report discusses the Selected Reserve, a group of over 811,000 part-time military personnel who can be called up for active duty in times of war or national emergency. About 91% of these reservists are part-time, and they train for about 1 weekend a month and 2 weeks a year. The report outlines the different types of training and duties required of reservists, including annual training, monthly drills, and active duty tours. Travel costs for reservists totaled over $925 million in fiscal year 2015, with an average cost of $1,246 per reservist. The report notes that some travel expenses are not reimbursed by the Department of Defense, and officials are considering changes to travel policy to address this issue. The report recommends that the Under Secretary of Defense for Personnel and Readiness collect more data and conduct an analysis of the impact of unreimbursed travel expenses on DOD's budget and readiness.",
